From 8b96bd47984b22aac9a74498ba0114f4175f6e6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:37:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] borg: record a visible Rune of Protection on the Borg's map

The Borg's map update set a grid's glyph flag only inside the branch for
visible, disarmable player traps.  A Rune of Protection (and a decoy) is
a glyph, not a player trap: its kind carries GLYPH | VISIBLE | FLOOR and
no TRAP flag, so that branch never ran for it and the Borg's map said
there was no rune on a grid that visibly had one.

Standing on such a rune with a summoner in view, the Borg's defence
choice therefore still saw the full summoning danger and read another
Rune of Protection onto the same grid, spending a scroll and a turn for
nothing.

Also enter the branch when the trap the player remembers on the grid
(map_info) is a glyph, and mark the grid as a trap only for a real
disarmable player trap.  The rune is then recorded and tracked as the
Borg's own runes are, and the Borg no longer reads a second rune on top
of it.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#295.

(cherry picked from commit 50e64a37a837c3ce4563e9ade452ce28db5cee82)
---
 src/borg/borg-update.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-update.c b/src/borg/borg-update.c
index 975ed846c..b88176a8b 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-update.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-update.c
@@ -328,12 +328,16 @@ static void borg_update_map(void)
 
             /* this checks that the trap is visible so it isn't really */
             /* a cheat of any information the borg couldn't get another way*/
-            } else if (square_isdisarmabletrap(cave, l)) {
+            /* A glyph (rune of protection) is not a player trap, so it is */
+            /* taken from the trap the player remembers on this grid. */
+            } else if (square_isdisarmabletrap(cave, l)
+                       || (g.trap && trf_has(g.trap->flags, TRF_GLYPH))) {
                 /* Minor cheat for the borg.  If the borg is running
                  * in the graphics mode (not the AdamBolt Tiles) he will
                  * mis-id the glyph of warding as a trap
                  */
-                ag->trap      = true;
+                if (square_isdisarmabletrap(cave, l))
+                    ag->trap = true;
                 uint8_t t_idx = square(cave, l)->trap->t_idx;
                 if (trf_has(trap_info[t_idx].flags, TRF_GLYPH)) {
                     ag->glyph = true;
